#!/usr/bin/env node
// Task studio-cosplay-general-20261108-225231-01 (lane COSTUME) — the FULL convention cosplay costumes: the eight Meshy T2.5 garment
// masters (Codex INITIAL concepts -> image-to-3D, generated by the primary; Meshy PBR maps kept) fitted to the zombie bodies head to toe,
// plus the convention head pieces (the mascot's bear-ear hat / wig, costume head, the sushi hat: build-cosplay.mjs's split + rigid fits)
// re-fitted to every costume body. CPU only, deterministic, no network / generation / inference.
//   node tools/asset-pipeline/zombie/build-cosplay-costumes.mjs     build and write
//        game/public/assets/models/outfit-cosplay-costume-head.glb   head slot: one wearable per costume, a variant per fitted body
//        game/public/assets/models/outfit-cosplay-costume-upper.glb  upper slot: the four jackets / tops (+ their Meshy maps)
//        game/public/assets/models/outfit-cosplay-costume-lower.glb  lower slot: the four skirts / trousers with legwear + footwear
//        game/public/assets/derivatives/outfit-cosplay-costume.json  provenance (sources, Meshy tasks, sha256), method, per body x clip
//                                                                  fit metrics, gate, bytes
//        game/src/ai/cosplayCostumes.generated.ts                  runtime table (files, bytes, wearables, costumes, fitted bodies)
//   --check    rebuild in a temp dir and require every output to be byte-identical (needs the private masters; without them: a
//              structural check of the shipped files against the recorded bytes / sha256)
//   dev only: --out=DIR, --costumes=a,b, --bodies=a,b, --step=0.2 (coarser validation), --no-gate
// Method: lib/costume-fit.mjs (parts, landmark retarget, interior caps, offset-field clearance through every validation pose, weights,
// masks), lib/costume-metrics.mjs (per clip poke-through / cloth-inside / coverage of the unclothed bodies), the head pieces from
// build-cosplay.mjs (+ the hat alone for long-haired bodies, fitted here).
